  "title": "isis-lsp: fix Coverity Overflowed constant",
  "description": "Fix Coverity Overflowed constant warning\n\nIn the loop, i runs from 0 to 31 (a total of 32 iterations).\n\n1. In the 32nd iteration (i = 31), the code successfully checks the 31st bit\n2. At the end of that same iteration, the mask shit is executed one last time.\n3. Since mask was already 2^31, shifting it left by 1 results in an overflow.\n\n**Solution:**\n\nShift inside the for expression. Handle the mask generation within the loop header itself.\n\nCoverity CID 1604195\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
